ons. Checked against git show HEAD (not the working tree), so this is not a local re-run artefact. PROTON: the block says the proton witness 'reports ord_{u=0}(tr_M(B_p)) = 19, matching 18*1 + 21*0 + 1 exactly'. computations/per-irrep-pole-proton-h3.witness.json contains {'name': 'full_tr_M_u_pole_eq_shift_NF_proton', 'computed': 18, 'expected': 19, 'passed': false} and 'allPassed': false. The computed value is 18, i.e. exactly the '+1' short. DEUTERON: the block says 'The per-term maximum is uniquely 40 at lambda = (4,1,1) (next-highest 39 at (4,2)); since the maximum is unique, lower-order terms cannot cancel it, so ord_{u=0}(tr_M(beta_D)) = 40 = 18*1 + 21*1 + 1 rigorously.' computations/per-irrep-pole-deuteron-h6.witness.json contains {'name': 'deuteron_full_tr_M_u_pole_eq_shift_NF', 'computed': 38, 'expected': 40, 'passed': false}, and its data.per_term_u_pole_orders give (4,2) -> 38, (3,3) -> 34, (5,1) -> 22, (6) -> 2, (4,1,1) -> 0, (3,2,1) -> 0. So EVERY number in that sentence disagrees with the witness: the maximising partition is (4,2), not (4,1,1); the maximum is 38, not 40; the runner-up is 34 at (3,3), not 39 at (4,2); and (4,1,1) \u2014 the partition the block names as the unique maximiser \u2014 has order 0, the joint minimum. Only the uniqueness itself survives ('deuteron_per_term_max_unique' passes), so the structural argument is sound but lands on 38, which is not 18+21+1. The parent .ts nonetheless carries computation.status: 'verified'. Proposed: treat the closed form as EMPIRICAL until the symbolic route is reconciled \u2014 note that the one witness that does pass, per-nucleon-shift-derivation.witness.json, labels its own assertions 'empirical from EMPIRICAL_SHIFT table (w3-w4 audit)', so nothing currently derives 18Z + 21N + 1; then either fix the two Path-A scripts or restate the block as reporting a 1-unit (proton) and 2-unit (deuteron) discrepancy, which is itself the interesting datum. (2) SWEEP DAMAGE, four sites in this one block: 'the canonical formalism' stands in for a script name at 'Each new generator's DP-max contribution to the q=0 pole is 1 (the canonical formalism)', at 'per the D(u) convention from the canonical formalism', and twice as the sole content of the 'Proton (A = 1, H_3): the canonical formalism' and 'Deuteron (A = 2, H_6): the canonical formalism' lines \u2014 where, from the witness filenames that follow, the intended names are per_irrep_pole_proton_h3.py and per_irrep_pole_deuteron_h6.py. Same token-substitution class already logged in this chapter's sidecars. (3) MINOR, scope: the parent states the closed form 'for all A >= 2', yet this proof verifies it at the proton, A = 1.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","model":null,"at":"2026-08-21","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"voice-agent-speak","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-extended.ts","model":null,"at":"2026-08-09","stale":false,"history":1},{"id":"voice-ai-slop","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"script","by":"content/p